cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or reference this software, please cite both the software (as
  below) and the accompanying dissertation under "preferred-citation".
title: >-
  EnergyView Evaluation: Prototype Study App for AI-Mediated
  Domestic Energy Interfaces
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nyree
    family-names: Marsh
    affiliation: University College London
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add once registered
abstract: >-
  Four interactive React prototypes operationalising Doran et al.'s (2017)
  explainability taxonomy as a controlled cumulative spectrum (interpretable
  baseline → comprehensible → uncertainty-integrated → truly explainable).
  Built as the research artefact for an undergraduate dissertation at
  University College London (BASC0024, May 2026), used in a scenario-based
  evaluation with non-technical participants to investigate how interface
  design can make autonomous AI energy decisions legible to everyday users.
keywords:
  - explainable AI
  - human-computer interaction
  - sustainable HCI
  - domestic energy
  - research through design
  - smart home
  - explainability
  - prototype evaluation
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nyreemarsh/basc0024-dissertation-prototypes"
url: "https://basc0024-dissertation-prototypes.vercel.app"
version: v1.0-dissertation
